      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T16:18:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, there is occasional interleaved output, but it\u0027s not because of anything in this CL.\n\nThis mutex is intended to solve accidental concurrent access to the circular buffer variables (i.e., by both a UART write and a snapshot command running at the same time).\n\nChanging printfs to not interleave would require mutexing at a different level (console_output.c, likely).",
      "parentUuid": "49dd7d5a_dcd4e8b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "2c329c68200f8e65115d598deeeebbe5d33c5d75",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
